  "difficultyRamp": {
    "within": "Q1 counts 6 ducks in twos. Child thinks in pairs, not one by one. Q2 counts 10 frame blocks in twos. Q3 continues 2, 4, 6 by adding 2. Q4 finds 6 in a twos gap. Q5 matches 8 to a pairs frame. Q6 counts hops of 2 to the mark at 8. Q7 reads 5 tens as 50. Q8 fills 40 in a tens column. Q9 picks two numbers from a tens count. Q10 orders 10, 20, 30, 40.",
    "versus": "Easy uses pairs and tens pictures up to 50, with hops on the number line. Medium adds fives, a twos gap, a tens pick and higher 5s counts. Hard names the step size, counts back, spots a number you would not say, and orders from biggest to smallest. Hard is a new kind of thinking, not just bigger numbers."
  },
